// Original ink-scribble heart marks — the same hand-carved-crosshatch
// technique as the icon set and the hero illustration (a dense field of
// short, jittered pen strokes clipped to a heart silhouette, plus a
// loose multi-pass sketch outline), generated fresh for this site
// rather than traced from any existing artwork or reference.
//
// Three variants, one job each:
//  - ScribbleHeart: the dense, strongest mark. For the one spot that
//    should anchor on a heart (site-footer.tsx's sign-off already
//    documents that job — this replaces IconHeartFilled there).
//  - ScribbleHeartLoose: sparser fill, quieter. For a background
//    watermark behind a heading, not a foreground mark.
//  - ScribbleHeartCluster: three small hearts, each its own layer, for
//    a scattered ambient accent (hero gutters, card grids).
//
// Colour via CSS custom properties (var(--accent)/var(--ink)) — same
// contract as LinocutIllustration — not currentColor, since these are
// always two-tone (red hatch + dark outline), never single-colour.
//
// Motion reuses existing keyframes rather than inventing new ones:
// heart-pulse already exists for exactly this "the heart mark beats"
// job (site-footer.tsx, page.tsx hero, trust/page.tsx), and
// lc-heart-outline-wobble's loose sketch-line drift is generic enough
// to reuse here even though its name comes from the hero illustration.
// ScribbleHeartLoose stays fully static, matching InkWash's own
// reasoning: a background texture shouldn't move.
//
// Static SVG counterparts (same artwork, portable/standalone, baked
// colours) live in public/illustrations/ for use outside the site.

